        "title": "ci(deadcode): restore enforced unused-export ratchet",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nThe unused-export baseline claimed that new entries fail CI, but the dependency shard stopped invoking `deadcode:exports` in #105704. At the same time, Knip's test-support exclusions lived under `ignoreFiles`, which only suppresses unused-file findings; unused exports and types from those files still inflated the baseline.\n\nRelated: #105575, #105595.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\n- Move test-support patterns to Knip's top-level `ignore`, while keeping production `live-*` files under `ignoreFiles` so their exports remain analyzed.\n- Restore `deadcode:exports` in the dependency shard. Current targets must provide the script; historical targets run it when their checkout supports it and otherwise retain the legacy fallback.\n- Add guard tests for the Knip option semantics and current/historical CI behavior.\n- Refresh the baseline from 5,705 entries on current `main` to 5,647 exact entries. This is configuration-driven cleanup plus a small hand-reviewed residue, not a mechanical export burn-down.\n- Preserve the shipped `packages/gateway-client` timeout export while removing its duplicate core re-export. Remove one obsolete session patch writer whose production callers had already migrated.\n- Classify fresh concurrent-main residue: internalize or delete nine genuinely private/dead exports, retain seven intentional test hooks in the baseline, and remove four now-live stale rows.\n\n## User Impact\n\nNo user-facing behavior change. CI now enforces that unused exports cannot grow silently, while intentional test and protocol surfaces remain intact.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- `pnpm deadcode:exports`: exact 5,647-entry match on Blacksmith Testbox `swift-crayfish-a34a` (`tbx_01kxcgvpqdnn3h0eg2dx3rg55w`).\n- Focused ratchet/gateway/session/plugin proof: 314 tests passed across six Vitest shards on `crimson-lobster-b31f`.\n- Focused auth/config/gateway/restart/plugin residue proof: 126 tests passed across six Vitest shards on `swift-crayfish-a34a`.\n- `pnpm build`: passed on Blacksmith Testbox `silver-shrimp-49a9`; Actions run https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/actions/runs/29216453346.\n- Broad `pnpm check:changed`: passed in Crabbox run `run_b800202102f3`.\n- Fresh autoreview: clean, no actionable findings (0.93 confidence).\n- `git diff --check`: clean.\n",
